  "143": {
    "inputs": {
      "value": "SCENE 4 — SORT WITH ORDER BY\n\n<Picture 1> defines <Subject 1>. Preserve the same character design.\n\nKeep the same hand-drawn 2D anime world.\n\n0:00-0:03:\nThe five Melbourne rows from the previous scene slide in from the LEFT and stop in the middle of the studio.\n\nEach row contains a clearly visible AGE value.\n\nFrom top to bottom, the exact ages are:\n\n42\n25\n37\n31\n29\n\nThe presenter looks at the messy order and shakes his head.\n\n<Subject 1> says:\n<d>[English, Neutral Filipino Male Voice] The right rows are here, but the order is messy.</d>\n\n0:03-0:06:\nA large hand-drawn downward arrow appears above the rows.\n\nExact uppercase text appears above the arrow:\n\nORDER BY AGE ASC\n\nThe rows physically rearrange themselves.\n\nAfter sorting, the ages must appear from top to bottom exactly as:\n\n25\n29\n31\n37\n42\n\nEach row lands into position with a soft CLICK sound.\n\n<Subject 1> says:\n<d>[English, Neutral Filipino Male Voice] ORDER BY can sort the results for you.</d>\n\n0:06-0:10:\nFast cut back to <Subject 1>.\n\nHe sweeps his right hand from left to right.\n\nBeside him, exact SQL text appears:\n\nORDER BY age ASC;\n\nDirectly underneath, a small horizontal label appears:\n\nASC = LOW TO HIGH\n\nThe presenter points downward at the five sorted ages.\n\n<Subject 1> says:\n<d>[English, Neutral Filipino Male Voice] ASC means ascending, so twenty-five comes before forty-two.</d>\n\nThe final sorted row transforms into a small illustrated card that flies toward the presenter’s opposite hand, setting up the next scene."
